{"availability":"available","full":"Walid-Idrissi-Labs/HueCtl","name":"HueCtl","description":"Turn any screen into a softbox, run from a control unit of knobs and keys: color temperature, tint, hue, saturation and a dimmer. One static page, no dependencies, works offline.","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-04-19T00:36:35Z","updated":"2026-10-11T19:17:00Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://huectl.vercel.app","topics":["color-temperature","lighting","offline-first","photography","pwa","softbox","vanilla-js","video-light"],"demo":"https://huectl.vercel.app/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T19:50:42.377Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T19:50:42.377Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T19:50:42.377Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T19:50:42.377Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Free and open source · runs in any current browser · installs to the home screen and works offline","HueCtl turns the screen in front of you into a softbox. Open the page and the whole screen becomes one even light: any white from the orange of an ember at 1500K to the blue of open sky at 9000K, or any color you turn it to. You run it from a control unit docked at the bottom of the screen, with knobs that turn and keys that travel, built to look and behave like the kit it stands beside. It is a single page with no dependencies, and it keeps working without a network."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Walid-Idrissi-Labs/HueCtl/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"2f7c15df805cebd1f9ed2438d98b093a8f4cb1d1f7d387deb984ec3d6931e401","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T19:50:42.492Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T19:50:42.492Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Free and open source · runs in any current browser · installs to the home screen and works offline","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Walid-Idrissi-Labs/HueCtl/blob/main/README.